WEBVTT

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:04.450
Gravel includes granules, pebbles, cobbles and boulders.

00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:07.890
Sand is finer than gravel, while silt and clay together make

00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:11.190
mud. The supplied size table gives the exact boundaries.

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:14.930
Clay is both a size term and a mineral-group name, so

00:00:14.930 --> 00:00:18.190
a clay-sized particle and a clay mineral describe different properties.

00:00:18.770 --> 00:00:21.570
Angular clasts have sharp edges and corners.

00:00:21.790 --> 00:00:25.790
Repeated collisions and abrasion tend to remove those exposed corners, producing

00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:28.670
smaller, rounder pieces. Shape is distinct from size:

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:31.450
a large cobble can be rounded, and a tiny sand grain

00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:35.470
can remain angular. Rounding does not by itself specify one transport

00:00:35.470 --> 00:00:35.910
distance.

00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:39.250
Poorly sorted sediment mixes many sizes.

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:43.670
Moderately sorted sediment has a more limited range, and well-sorted sediment

00:00:43.670 --> 00:00:49.190
concentrates similar sizes. Wind-built dunes commonly contain well-sorted sand because wind

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:52.570
cannot supply gravel and finer particles may move onward.

00:00:52.710 --> 00:00:55.230
A mixture can be rounded and still poorly sorted.

00:00:55.870 --> 00:01:00.130
Near a bedrock source, sediment commonly starts coarse, angular and poorly

00:01:00.130 --> 00:01:03.810
sorted. Transport can break it, round it and separate sizes.

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:08.110
Farther along a stream or repeatedly worked by waves, finer and

00:01:08.110 --> 00:01:12.730
better-sorted material may remain. These are useful tendencies whose interpretation still

00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:15.070
depends on source rocks and available sediment.

00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:18.050
The textbook identifies four controls:

00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:22.650
slope steepness, current strength, sediment supply and the transporting agent.

00:01:22.990 --> 00:01:27.350
Strong turbulent water can move larger clasts than weaker flow, but

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:30.410
it cannot carry a size the source does not provide.

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:34.150
Glaciers can move large mixtures, while wind is selective.

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:38.350
Describe size, roundness and sorting before interpreting the setting.
